{"meta":{"format_version":"5.0","model_format":"free","box_uv":false},"name":"wall_corner_stone_broken","model_identifier":"wall_corner_stone_broken","visible_box":[1,1,0],"variable_placeholders":"","multi_file_ruleset":"","variable_placeholder_buttons":[],"timeline_setups":[],"unhandled_root_fields":{"description":"# wall_corner_stone_broken\n\nDamaged state below 40 % HP of `wall_corner_stone` (Patch 5): the stone piece snapped in half, with splinters (or broken stone) at the break and the upper half (group `hanging_half`) still attached by a thread, hanging down to rest on the ground in front (-Z). Purely visual: the hanging half does not block movement and the wall works the same. The game swaps it in below 40 % HP and back to `wall_corner_stone_cracked` when repaired above 40 %.\n\nStone wall corner: an L joint filling one column; walls leave along -X... +X (north face) and along +Z (west face), with a corner post.\n\n- Footprint: 1 x 1 columns (16 x 16 units, 0.45 x 0.45 m), centred on the origin, front (door side) faces -Z.\n- Finished bounds: x -15..15, y 0..69, z -63..8 units.\n- Texture: 256 x 128, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering, flat pixel-art tones per material (repainted in Patch 5 for colour contrast).\n- Cubes: 19, all in `finished`; the construction and ruined state sets and the damaged/abandoned texture variants were removed in Patch 5 (the game draws none of them for buildings).\n\n## Hit box\n\n- 16 x 128 x 16 centred at the origin"},"resolution":{"width":256,"height":128},"elements":[{"name":"stone_merlon_n#aba79d","box_uv":false,"render_order":"default","locked":false,"export":true,"scope":0,"allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[-8,118,-8],"to":[0,128,-4],"autouv":0,"color":0,"origin":[0,0,0],"faces":{"north":{"uv":[186,66,194,76],"texture":0},"east":{"uv":[218,66,222,76],"texture":0},"south":{"uv":[194,66,202,76],"texture":0},"west":{"uv":[222,66,226,76],"texture":0},"up":{"uv":[88,120,96,124],"texture":0},"down":{"uv":[96,120,1